  whyItMatters:"Seeds decide a crop's yield before any chemical is sprayed, and hybrid and GM seed is protected by breeding know-how, so returns are high when a hybrid wins share. Cotton seed prices are capped by the government, and new GM traits need regulatory approval, which shapes who can grow.",
  valuePoolDescription:"Hybrid maize, rice and vegetable seed earn the best margins; Bt cotton seed is price-capped. Advanta (UPL) is the largest Indian-origin seed company abroad. Specialty nutrition is small but unsubsidised, so its makers keep pricing power.",
